WEBVTT

00:00.501 --> 00:01.511
- [Voiceover] What I
hope to do in this video,

00:01.511 --> 00:03.473
is give ourselves some practice

00:03.473 --> 00:05.400
interpreting statements

00:05.400 --> 00:08.244
and writing them as
mathematical expressions,

00:08.244 --> 00:11.100
possibly using parentheses.

00:11.100 --> 00:12.308
So let's get started.

00:12.308 --> 00:13.914
And for any of these statements,

00:13.914 --> 00:14.952
if you get so inspired,

00:14.952 --> 00:17.033
and I encourage you to get so inspired,

00:17.033 --> 00:18.937
pause the video and see
if you can write them

00:18.937 --> 00:21.294
as mathematical expressions.

00:21.294 --> 00:22.339
So this first one says

00:22.339 --> 00:26.867
700 minus 19, divided in half.

00:26.867 --> 00:28.017
So we could say,

00:28.017 --> 00:29.293
another way to think about divided in half

00:29.293 --> 00:31.476
is divided by two,

00:31.476 --> 00:32.904
so we could write this as

00:32.904 --> 00:37.362
709 minus 19,

00:37.362 --> 00:38.941
and we're going to do that first,

00:38.941 --> 00:41.333
so that's why I put the
parentheses around it,

00:41.333 --> 00:45.311
divided by two, or divided in half.

00:45.311 --> 00:48.276
That's one way that we could write this.

00:48.276 --> 00:49.367
Now the next one,

00:49.367 --> 00:51.434
and once again, pause
it if you get inspired,

00:51.434 --> 00:52.769
and I encourage you to.

00:52.769 --> 00:57.471
Three times the sum of 56 and seven.

00:57.471 --> 00:59.433
So it's gonna be three times

00:59.433 --> 01:01.070
the sum of 56 and seven.

01:01.070 --> 01:02.428
So the sum of 56 and seven,

01:02.428 --> 01:04.135
we want to take that first,

01:04.135 --> 01:07.188
so it's going to be 56 plus the seven,

01:07.188 --> 01:10.695
that's the sum of 56 and seven,

01:10.695 --> 01:13.432
and then we want to do three times that.

01:13.432 --> 01:16.198
We want to do three times this sum.

01:16.198 --> 01:19.727
So we could write it like that.

01:19.727 --> 01:20.900
Another way we could write it,

01:20.900 --> 01:22.235
when you're dealing with parentheses,

01:22.235 --> 01:23.709
and you're going to see this more and more

01:23.709 --> 01:26.856
as you get into more
and more fancy algebra,

01:26.856 --> 01:27.506
I guess you could say,

01:27.506 --> 01:29.683
but what I'm about to
show you isn't so fancy,

01:29.683 --> 01:32.034
is, you don't have to write
the multiplication sign here.

01:32.034 --> 01:35.505
You could just write three,
and then open parentheses,

01:35.505 --> 01:37.542
56 plus seven,

01:41.896 --> 01:44.368
and this, too, is three times

01:44.368 --> 01:47.410
the sum of 56 and seven.

01:47.410 --> 01:48.733
And you want to be very careful,

01:48.733 --> 01:50.904
because you might be
tempted to maybe do it

01:50.904 --> 01:51.934
without the parentheses,

01:51.934 --> 01:53.993
so you might be tempted
to do something like this,

01:53.993 --> 01:55.853
three times

01:56.992 --> 02:01.335
56 plus seven,

02:01.335 --> 02:02.844
but this one isn't, obviously,

02:02.844 --> 02:05.422
three times the sum of 56 and seven.

02:05.422 --> 02:07.337
In fact, the standard
way to interpret this

02:07.337 --> 02:09.334
is that you would do the
multiplication first.

02:09.334 --> 02:11.134
You would do three times 56,

02:11.134 --> 02:12.504
and then add seven,

02:12.504 --> 02:13.804
which is going to give
you a different value,

02:13.804 --> 02:15.035
and you could try it out,

02:15.035 --> 02:18.065
than if you were to add
the 56 and the seven first.

02:18.065 --> 02:21.020
So, to make sure that you do
the 56 and the seven first,

02:21.020 --> 02:24.102
you want to put this
parentheses around it.

02:24.102 --> 02:25.867
So let's keep going.

02:25.867 --> 02:30.789
The sum of three times 56 and seven.

02:30.789 --> 02:33.517
So we're gonna take the sum of two things.

02:35.640 --> 02:37.709
The first thing that we're
gonna take the sum of

02:37.709 --> 02:40.577
is three times 56.

02:40.577 --> 02:44.303
So, three times 56,

02:44.303 --> 02:46.168
and seven.

02:47.768 --> 02:49.342
Let me do that in a different color.

02:49.342 --> 02:51.392
And seven.

02:53.069 --> 02:54.779
So this right over here is the sum

02:54.779 --> 02:57.701
of three times 56, and seven.

02:57.701 --> 02:59.443
Now it's always good to
write the parentheses.

02:59.443 --> 03:01.363
It makes it a little bit cleaner,

03:01.363 --> 03:02.798
a little bit more obvious.

03:02.798 --> 03:05.373
Look, I'm gonna take the three times 56,

03:05.373 --> 03:06.571
I'm gonna do that first,

03:06.571 --> 03:08.011
and then I'm gonna add seven,

03:08.011 --> 03:09.300
but based on what I just told you,

03:09.300 --> 03:11.807
the standard way, if
someone were to just write

03:11.807 --> 03:16.734
three times 56 plus seven,

03:26.763 --> 03:28.855
this actually can still be interpreted as

03:28.855 --> 03:32.004
the sum of three times 56, and seven,

03:32.004 --> 03:33.304
because as I just said,

03:33.304 --> 03:35.644
the standard, the convention, so to speak,

03:35.644 --> 03:37.774
is to do your multiplication first.

03:37.774 --> 03:39.794
Order of operations,
which you may or may not,

03:39.794 --> 03:42.407
if you're not familiar, you
will be familiar with it soon,

03:42.407 --> 03:44.322
is to do the multiplication first,

03:44.322 --> 03:47.271
and then add the seven,
or then do the addition.

03:47.271 --> 03:48.444
But just to make it clear,

03:48.444 --> 03:51.068
it doesn't hurt to put
the parentheses there.

03:51.068 --> 03:54.469
Three times 56, plus seven.

03:54.469 --> 03:56.701
Now we have 43

03:56.701 --> 04:00.826
minus the sum of 16 and 11.

04:01.103 --> 04:03.569
So, 43 minus,

04:03.569 --> 04:06.100
so we're gonna have 43 minus,

04:06.100 --> 04:09.200
minus the sum of 16 and 11.

04:09.200 --> 04:12.636
So, minus the sum of 16 and 11.

04:12.636 --> 04:14.738
So, from 43, we're gonna take

04:14.738 --> 04:19.068
the sum of 16 and 11,

04:19.068 --> 04:20.996
and so, once again, the
parentheses make it clear

04:20.996 --> 04:23.422
that we're going to take
the sum of 16 and 11,

04:23.422 --> 04:25.535
and we're gonna take that from 43.

04:25.535 --> 04:28.043
The parentheses are very,
very, very important here,

04:28.043 --> 04:31.133
because if we just did 43

04:32.303 --> 04:35.165
minus 16

04:36.704 --> 04:38.376
plus 11,

04:38.376 --> 04:39.966
the standard way of
interpreting this would be

04:39.966 --> 04:43.310
43 minus 16, and then adding 11,

04:43.310 --> 04:45.074
which would give you
a different value than

04:45.074 --> 04:48.225
43 minus the sum of 16 and 11.

04:48.225 --> 04:49.277
So once again, the parentheses

04:49.277 --> 04:51.530
are very, very, very important here

04:51.530 --> 04:55.396
to make it clear that you're
gonna add the 16 and 11 first,

04:55.396 --> 04:59.808
and then subtract that sum from 43.

04:59.808 --> 05:02.002
This is fun, let's keep going.

05:02.002 --> 05:06.448
10 times the quotient of 104 and eight.

05:06.448 --> 05:09.003
So, we're gonna do 10 times something.

05:09.003 --> 05:11.498
10 times the quotient

05:11.498 --> 05:14.301
of 104 and eight,

05:14.301 --> 05:18.105
and so the quotient of 104 and
8 we could write like this,

05:18.105 --> 05:20.391
104

05:20.391 --> 05:24.940
divided by eight,

05:24.940 --> 05:27.137
or, based on what we told
you a little earlier,

05:27.137 --> 05:28.101
you could write this as

05:28.101 --> 05:31.288
10 times the quotient

05:31.735 --> 05:35.589
of 104 and eight,

05:35.589 --> 05:40.210
or 104 divided by eight.

05:40.210 --> 05:41.870
Now let's just do this last one.

05:41.870 --> 05:44.110
Four times as large

05:48.662 --> 05:50.629
as the expression

05:52.029 --> 05:55.416
175 minus 58.

05:55.416 --> 05:57.602
So I'm gonna do four times
as large as something,

05:57.602 --> 06:00.364
so I'm gonna multiply
something times four.

06:00.934 --> 06:02.443
It's four times as large as the expression

06:02.443 --> 06:05.648
175 minus 58.

06:08.295 --> 06:10.756
And once again, I could write it as

06:10.756 --> 06:13.918
four times as large

06:13.918 --> 06:15.539
as the expression,

06:15.539 --> 06:17.304
let me do that in that purple color,

06:17.304 --> 06:20.207
as the expression

06:20.207 --> 06:22.037
175

06:22.037 --> 06:26.745
minus 58.

06:26.745 --> 06:27.962
Either way,

06:27.962 --> 06:30.238
and once again, if you
were to do it like this,

06:30.238 --> 06:32.699
if you didn't write the parentheses,

06:32.699 --> 06:34.835
then, it wouldn't be the same thing,

06:34.835 --> 06:36.333
'cause if the parentheses weren't here,

06:36.333 --> 06:38.666
then you would want to do
the four times 175 first,

06:38.666 --> 06:40.052
and then subtract the 58,

06:40.052 --> 06:42.695
which isn't what this
statement is telling us.

06:42.695 --> 06:44.193
And this last one, I think,

06:44.193 --> 06:46.944
brings up an interesting
thing for us to think about,

06:46.944 --> 06:50.195
because if someone were to
walk up to you on the street,

06:50.195 --> 06:51.809
and they were to show you--

06:51.809 --> 06:54.073
Whoops, what's going on with my computer?

06:54.073 --> 06:55.443
And they were to show you

06:55.443 --> 06:57.484
two different expressions.

06:57.484 --> 07:01.167
Well, the first expression said two--

07:01.167 --> 07:01.798
Let's write it this way,

07:01.798 --> 07:03.017
actually, I'm not gonna
even speak 'em out.

07:03.017 --> 07:05.207
I'm just gonna write it down.

07:05.207 --> 07:09.895
I'm just gonna write
some crazy number here.

07:10.942 --> 07:15.737
Some crazy numbers here.

07:15.737 --> 07:18.001
So that's one expression

07:18.001 --> 07:19.766
that someone were to write,

07:19.766 --> 07:22.574
and let's say another one is this one,

07:24.236 --> 07:25.861
and I'm intentionally--

07:25.861 --> 07:27.907
What, I put the commas in the wrong place.

07:27.907 --> 07:30.273
Let me make sure I get this right.

07:30.273 --> 07:32.502
Alright, that's 183,576.

07:32.502 --> 07:34.998
This is 37,399.

07:34.998 --> 07:36.403
So that's one expression,

07:36.403 --> 07:38.678
and then another expression is this.

07:39.770 --> 07:43.473
And I'm intentionally not reading it out.

07:43.473 --> 07:44.402
Well, I'll read it out a little bit,

07:44.402 --> 07:46.736
37,399.

07:46.736 --> 07:48.094
And someone said, "Quick!

07:48.094 --> 07:50.555
"Which expression is larger?"

07:50.555 --> 07:51.635
And you might be tempted,

07:51.635 --> 07:52.703
or you might not be tempted,

07:52.703 --> 07:53.342
but you might be tempted,

07:53.342 --> 07:54.712
"Oh, let me calculate this thing.

07:54.712 --> 07:56.268
"Gee, I'm gonna have to
write this thing down,

07:56.268 --> 07:58.092
"or use a calculator or something,

07:58.092 --> 07:59.309
"or whatever else to add

07:59.309 --> 08:03.265
"183,576

08:03.265 --> 08:05.208
"plus 37,399,

08:05.208 --> 08:06.690
"and then I'm gonna have
to multiply that by two,

08:06.690 --> 08:08.934
"and figure out what
that number is equal to,

08:08.934 --> 08:09.770
"and then I would have to take

08:09.770 --> 08:13.555
"183,576 plus 37,399

08:13.555 --> 08:14.530
"and figure out what that is,

08:14.530 --> 08:15.900
"multiply that by seven,

08:15.900 --> 08:17.131
"and figure out what that's going to be.

08:17.131 --> 08:17.967
"That's hard!

08:17.967 --> 08:18.605
"That's gonna take--"

08:18.605 --> 08:20.207
Not hard, it's just
gonna take you some time,

08:20.207 --> 08:22.239
you might make some careless mistakes.

08:22.239 --> 08:23.470
But the big realization to say,

08:23.470 --> 08:25.107
"Well, which one is larger?

08:25.107 --> 08:27.069
"Well I don't have to even
calculate these things!"

08:27.069 --> 08:31.202
'Cause this is two times this
craziness right over here,

08:31.202 --> 08:33.570
this thing that's gonna
be 200 something thousand,

08:33.570 --> 08:35.277
and this is seven times that thing

08:35.277 --> 08:38.540
that is going to be 200
and something thousand.

08:38.540 --> 08:39.770
So seven times that thing

08:39.770 --> 08:42.777
is going to be larger
than two times that thing,

08:42.777 --> 08:44.003
and so, one way to--

08:44.003 --> 08:46.504
Before you dive deep, and
start computing things,

08:46.504 --> 08:48.176
it's always good to take
a step back and say,

08:48.176 --> 08:51.102
"Hey, look, can I look at how
the expressions are formed,

08:51.102 --> 08:53.075
"the structure of these expressions?"

08:53.075 --> 08:56.442
And say, "Look, this is
two times this thing,

08:56.442 --> 08:58.543
"and this is seven times this thing."

08:58.543 --> 09:00.413
Well, the seven is going to be,

09:00.413 --> 09:03.372
this one right over here is going to be

09:03.741 --> 09:06.126
a larger expression.

09:06.126 --> 09:07.934
Anyway, hopefully you enjoyed that

09:07.934 --> 09:09.703
as much as I did.
